"code> &rarr; expect HTTP 200 with image content-type."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:188
msgid "Rebuild + Deploy Now."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:189
msgid ""
"View source of any deployed post &rarr; <code>og:image</code>, JSON-LD "
"<code>image</code>/<code>logo</code>, and <code>&lt;img src&gt;</code> all "
"reference your live host (<code>example.com</code>), not the dashboard."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:193
msgid ""
"<strong>If the toggle is on but proxy is NOT set up:</strong> every image / "
"theme stylesheet / plugin script on the live site will return 404. Verify "
"the curl test above before flipping the toggle on a production site."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:198
msgid "Bundle <code>/wp-content/uploads/</code> into deploy (shared hosting)"
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:200
msgid ""
"Use this when the Worker / Nginx proxy approach above doesn't work because "
"your origin's firewall blocks Cloudflare. Common on shared cPanel hosts "
"(HostArmada, SiteGround, GoDaddy, Bluehost, etc.) where you can't whitelist "
"Cloudflare's edge IPs. Symptoms: <code>curl -I https://example.com/wp-"
"content/uploads/file.jpg</code> returns <code>HTTP/1.1 520</code> or "
"<code>522</code> while the direct dashboard URL works."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:203
msgid "What it does"
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:205
msgid ""
"Tick <strong>Export Scope &rarr; Bundle <code>/wp-content/uploads/</code> "
"into deploy</strong> (leave <strong>Rewrite <code>/wp-content/</code> URLs</"
"strong> off). On the next rebuild the plugin:"
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:208
msgid ""
"Scans every rendered page for <code>/wp-content/uploads/...</code> "
"references &mdash; <code>&lt;img src&gt;</code>, <code>srcset</code>, "
"<code>og:image</code>, JSON-LD <code>image</code>/<code>logo</code>/"
"<code>thumbnailUrl</code>, inline CSS <code>url(...)</code>, oEmbed "
"thumbnails (literal, JSON-escaped, and percent-encoded forms)."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:209
msgid "Fetches each unique file from the WordPress origin during rebuild."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:210
msgid ""
"Uploads them inside the Cloudflare Pages deploy at their original <code>/wp-"
"content/uploads/...</code> paths."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:211
msgid ""
"Rewrites image URLs in the rendered HTML / JSON-LD to the live host so the "
"static site is fully self-contained."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:214
msgid "What still loads from origin"
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:216
msgid ""
"Theme CSS/JS and plugin assets (everything under <code>/wp-content/themes/</"
"code> and <code>/wp-content/plugins/</code>) keep loading from the WordPress "
"dashboard host as before. Those rarely cause shared-hosting firewall issues, "
"and bundling them on every deploy would balloon the upload size for no SEO "
"benefit."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:219
msgid "Cost / size considerations"
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:221
msgid ""
"Only files <em>referenced</em> from exported pages get bundled &mdash; not "
"the entire media library. Cloudflare's <code>check-missing</code> API "
"deduplicates unchanged files by content hash, so subsequent rebuilds only "
"upload new or modified images. If your origin uses <a href=\"https://"
"wordpress.org/plugins/webp-express/\" target=\"_blank\" "
"rel=\"noopener\">WebP Express</a> or similar (serving <code>.webp</code> via "
"headers), the plugin captures whichever extension your origin actually "
"returns in the rendered HTML."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:224
msgid "Verify after deploy"
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:226
msgid ""
"Watch the activity log &mdash; expect <code>Bundling N /wp-content/uploads/ "
"file(s) into deploy...</code> then <code>Asset bundle done: X ok, Y failed, "
"Z MB total</code>."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:227
msgid ""
"<code>curl -I https://example.com/wp-content/uploads/<em>any-file</em>.jpg</"
"code> &rarr; expect <code>HTTP/1.1 200 OK</code> with <code>Server: "
"cloudflare</code> and a <code>cf-ray</code> header (served by CF Pages "
"directly, not your origin)."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:228
msgid ""
"View any deployed post source &rarr; <code>og:image</code>, JSON-LD image "
"fields, and <code>&lt;img src&gt;</code> / <code>srcset</code> all point at "
"the live host."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:232
msgid ""
"<strong>Which option do I pick?</strong> If your origin proxies cleanly "
"through Cloudflare (VPS / dedicated / fully managed with Worker route "
"accepting CF subrequests), use the Worker/Nginx proxy above &mdash; uploads "
"stay on the dashboard, deploys stay tiny. If your origin is shared hosting "
"and you keep getting 520/522 from the Worker route, use this bundle option "
"instead."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:236
msgid ""
"<strong>Ignored when \"Rewrite <code>/wp-content/</code> URLs\" is on.</"
"strong> That setting rewrites everything (themes, plugins, uploads) and "
"assumes you have a full proxy. The bundle option only matters when the "
"broader rewrite toggle is off."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:242
msgid ""
"Grouped by where it happens. The <code>code-styled</code> phrases are the "
"exact <strong>Activity Log</strong> messages, so you can match what you see."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:244
msgid "Login &amp; DNS cutover"
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:246
msgid ""
"After DNS cutover, wp-admin bounces to the live site — can't log in or "
"redeploy"
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:248
msgid ""
"<strong>Symptom:</strong> opening wp-admin throws you to the <em>public</em> "
"host's login, e.g. <code>https://example.com/wp-login.php?"
"redirect_to=https%3A%2F%2Fdashboard.example.com%2Fwp-admin%2F...</code> — "
"but <code>example.com</code> is now the static Cloudflare site with no "
"WordPress on it, so login fails and you can't reach this page to redeploy."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:249
msgid ""
"<strong>Cause:</strong> WordPress's own <strong>WP Address</strong> "
"(<code>siteurl</code>) / <strong>Site Address</strong> (<code>home</code>) "
"still point at the public host instead of your dashboard host. WordPress "
"builds the login URL from <code>siteurl</code>, so it sends you to the "
"static site."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:250
msgid ""
"<strong>Fix:</strong> pin both to the dashboard host in <code>wp-config.php</"
"code> (add just above <code>/* That's all, stop editing! Happy publishing. */"
"</code>):"
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:253
msgid ""
"Save, then log in from a private/incognito window at <code>https://"
"dashboard.example.com/wp-admin</code>."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:255
msgid ""
"<strong>Keep them separate:</strong> WordPress lives on "
"<code>dashboard.example.com</code>; the plugin's <strong>Public Site URL</"
"strong> stays the public host (<code>https://example.com</code>). The "
"renderer rewrites the dashboard host &rarr; Public Site URL during export, "
"so the static site still shows clean public links. Only WordPress's own two "
"addresses move to the dashboard subdomain — never the plugin's Public Site "
"URL."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:260
msgid "Setup &amp; connection (Test Connection)"
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:263
msgid ""
"One of the three credential fields is blank. Fill Account ID, API Token, and "
"Pages Project, Save, then test again."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:266
msgid ""
"The <strong>Pages Project</strong> field must be the project <em>slug</em> "
"only (e.g. <code>mysite</code>), never the full <code>mysite.pages.dev</"
"code> URL. Also confirm the project lives in the <em>same</em> Cloudflare "
"account whose Account ID you pasted."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:268
msgid "<code>Test FAIL</code> with an authentication / HTTP 403 message"
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:269
msgid ""
"The API token is wrong, expired, or under-scoped. Create one with exactly "
"<strong>Account &middot; Cloudflare Pages &middot; Edit</strong> and "
"<em>Account Resources</em> including the right account, re-paste it (it's "
"shown only once at creation), and Save."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:272
msgid ""
"The connection can test OK with a read-only token, but deploying needs write "
"access. Recreate the token with <strong>Cloudflare Pages &middot; Edit</"
"strong> (not Read)."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:275
msgid "Rebuild won't start or won't finish"
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:277
msgid "\"Rebuild + Deploy Now\" or auto-deploy does nothing — no new log lines"
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:278
msgid ""
"The rebuild runs on a WordPress scheduled event a few seconds after you "
"click, so it depends on <strong>WP-Cron</strong>. If <code>DISABLE_WP_CRON</"
"code> is defined, or the site gets almost no traffic, the event may never "
"fire — you'll see <code>Full rebuild queued (manual).</code> but never "
"<code>Full rebuild started.</code> Fixes: load any front-end page to nudge "
"WP-Cron, or run a real system cron hitting <code>wp-cron.php</code> every "
"minute."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:281
msgid ""
"No post types are ticked under <strong>Export Scope</strong>, or nothing is "
"published in the selected types. Tick at least one post type (and/or "
"Homepage / Taxonomies / Authors) and confirm you have published content."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:284
msgid ""
"The plugin fetches your own URLs via <code>wp_remote_get</code>. A handful "
"of failures is usually harmless; many means the site is blocking itself — "
"HTTP basic auth, an IP allow-list, an aggressive WAF, Cloudflare \"Under "
"Attack\" mode, or a coming-soon / maintenance plugin. Let the origin fetch "
"itself (or pause the blocker during deploys). For an invalid / self-signed "
"origin cert during migration, add <code>add_filter( 'sforge_sslverify', "
"'__return_false' );</code>."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:287
msgid ""
"Every page failed to render, so there was nothing to upload — almost always "
"the same self-fetch block as above. Check the <code>Render fail</code> lines "
"just above this one for the HTTP code."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:289
msgid ""
"Stuck on <code>Hashing files...</code> / <code>Manifest: ... files</code>"
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:290
msgid ""
"PHP ran out of memory or hit the time limit while encoding the upload. The "
"plugin already requests <code>set_time_limit(0)</code> and "
"<code>memory_limit 512M</code>, but shared hosts can override that. Raise "
"<code>memory_limit</code> (256&ndash;512MB) and <code>max_execution_time</"
"code> via <code>php.ini</code> or your host panel."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:293
msgid "Deploy step errors (Cloudflare API)"
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:296
msgid ""
"An old build sent the deployment as URL-encoded form data. v1.0.0+ sends "
"<code>multipart/form-data</code>, which Cloudflare requires — update the "
"plugin."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:299
msgid ""
"Usually a single file over Cloudflare Pages' <strong>25&nbsp;MiB</strong> "
"per-file limit (a large video / PDF in uploads), or a network timeout on a "
"big batch. Remove or relocate oversized media and host it elsewhere."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:302
msgid ""
"A Cloudflare-side rejection; the exact reason is quoted in the log. Common "
"cause: more than <strong>20,000 files</strong> in one deployment (CF Pages "
"free-tier limit). Trim Export Scope, or split a very large site."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:305
msgid ""
"A transient Cloudflare API hiccup or a token problem mid-deploy. Re-run "
"<strong>Rebuild + Deploy Now</strong>; if it persists, re-test the "
"connection — the token may have been revoked."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:308
msgid "Live site looks wrong"
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:310
msgid "Images broken on the live site (or only <em>some</em> show)"
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:311
msgid ""
"By default <code>/wp-content/*</code> URLs (including uploads) keep pointing "
"at your WordPress origin, so the origin must be reachable over HTTPS with a "
"valid cert — proxy that subdomain through Cloudflare (orange cloud) so CF "
"serves a fresh edge cert. If your host blocks Cloudflare (<code>520</code> / "
"<code>522</code> on uploads), tick <strong>Bundle <code>/wp-content/uploads/"
"</code> into deploy</strong> so images ship inside the deploy. If only "
"<em>some</em> broke right after a cutover, it's usually a stale deploy plus "
"a wrong <strong>Site Address</strong> (see <em>Login &amp; DNS cutover</em> "
"above) — fix that, then Rebuild + Deploy Now."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:313
msgid "<code>&lt;project&gt;.pages.dev</code> doesn't redirect to my domain"
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:314
msgid ""
"The redirect is a client-side JS snippet (the Direct Upload API can't run "
"<code>_worker.js</code> / Functions), so <code>curl -I</code> won't show it "
"— test in a real browser. It only fires when <strong>Public Site URL</"
"strong> is a real domain (not a <code>.pages.dev</code> URL) and the "
"<strong>Redirect *.pages.dev to live host</strong> toggle is on."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:316
msgid "Live site shows <code>noindex</code>"
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:317
msgid ""
"WordPress &rarr; Settings &rarr; Reading: leave <strong>\"Discourage search "
"engines\"</strong> UNCHECKED on the dashboard. The plugin scrubs "
"<code>noindex</code> / <code>nofollow</code> meta during render, but that "
"toggle also changes how SEO plugins build the sitemap."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:319
msgid "Contact forms don't send on the live site"
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:320
msgid ""
"Cloudflare Pages is static — no PHP / WordPress runtime — so anything "
"posting to <code>admin-ajax.php</code> or <code>/wp-json/</code> (Contact "
"Form 7, WPForms, Gravity Forms) silently fails. Point the form at a static-"
"friendly endpoint (a Cloudflare Pages Function / Worker, Formspree, Basin, "
"Web3Forms). A form posting to a <em>different</em> host is left untouched "
"and keeps working."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:322
msgid "Duplicate SEO meta or schema in <code>&lt;head&gt;</code>"
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:323
msgid ""
"An SEO plugin we don't auto-detect is also injecting tags. Two-tier dedup "
"covers Yoast, Rank Math, AIO SEO, SEOPress, The SEO Framework, Slim SEO, "
"Squirrly, SmartCrawl, WP Meta SEO (general SEO plugins → all injection "
"paused) and Schema &amp; Structured Data for WP &amp; AMP, Schema Pro, "
"WPSSO, Schema by Hesham, Schema App, Magazine3 Schema (schema-only plugins → "
"only JSON-LD paused). For niche plugins, extend detection via the "
"<code>sforge_seo_competing_plugin</code> or "
"<code>sforge_schema_competing_plugin</code> filter, or simply untick "
"<strong>Inject SEO meta</strong>."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:325
msgid "FAQ / HowTo schema not appearing"
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:326
msgid ""
"FAQ schema needs Yoast / Rank Math / SEOPress FAQ blocks OR "
"<code>&lt;details&gt;&lt;summary&gt;Question&lt;/summary&gt;Answer&lt;/"
"details&gt;</code> markup in the content. HowTo needs a Yoast or Rank Math "
"HowTo block, OR a title starting with \"How to\" + a numbered list with 3+ "
"items. Use the <code>sforge_faq_items</code> / <code>sforge_howto_data</"
"code> filters to inject manually."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:329
msgid "Sitemaps &amp; multilingual"
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:331
msgid "Sub-sitemaps missing on deploy"
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:332
msgid ""
"v1.0.0+ handles CDATA-wrapped <code>&lt;loc&gt;</code> entries in sitemap-"
"index files. Earlier builds skipped them — update and redeploy."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:335
msgid ""
"Your origin exposes no sitemap, so the plugin tried to generate one — but "
"everything is unticked under <strong>Sitemap Generator</strong>. Tick at "
"least one post type / Homepage / Taxonomies / Authors."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:338
msgid ""
"The generator ran but matched no published URLs. Confirm you have published "
"content in the selected sitemap post types."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:340
msgid "TranslatePress languages aren't on the live site"
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:341
msgid ""
"If the log notes that secondary languages are on <strong>separate "
"subdomains / domains</strong>, that's expected — one Cloudflare Pages "
"project serves one hostname. Switch TranslatePress to <strong>subdirectory</"
"strong> mode (<code>/fr/</code>, <code>/de/</code>) and Rebuild; all "
"languages then ship in the one deploy."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:344
msgid ""
"An image optimiser is swapping image URLs with JavaScript (e.g. EWWW "
"<strong>Lazy Load</strong> or <strong>Easy IO</strong>), so the real URLs "
"aren't in the rendered HTML for the bundler to find. Turn off the JS lazy-"
"load / Easy-IO feature (keep the compression) and Rebuild."
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:347
msgid "Limits &amp; frequency"
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:349
msgid "Hit ~100 deployments per day"
msgstr ""

#: admin/help-page.php:350
msgid ""
"Free Cloudflare Pages tier soft cap. Raise the plugin's <em>Debounce</em> "
"setting from 120s to e.g. 600s so rapid bulk edits collapse into fewer "
"deploys."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: plugin version, 2: author name linked to their website.
#: admin/help-page.php:357
#, php-format
msgid ""
"<strong>StaticForge for Cloudflare Pages</strong> v%1$s &mdash; built by %2$s"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:25
msgid ""
"Auto-export your WordPress site as static HTML &mdash; deploy to Cloudflare "
"Pages on every publish."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:37
msgid "<strong>Connection OK.</strong> Cloudflare Pages project is reachable."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:39
msgid ""
"<strong>Connection failed.</strong> See the activity log below for details."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:41
msgid ""
"<strong>Full rebuild queued.</strong> The activity log refreshes live "
"&mdash; watch for progress in the next few seconds."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:48
msgid "First time? Read the Setup Guide."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:49
msgid ""
"Walk-through for creating a Cloudflare Pages project, generating an API "
"token, and configuring this plugin."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:51
msgid "Open Setup Guide"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:62
msgid "Cloudflare"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:63
msgid "Connect to your Cloudflare Pages project via the Direct Upload API."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:71
msgid "e.g. a2709493ed708e84df53c91fa354c230"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:72
msgid ""
"Cloudflare Dashboard &rarr; right sidebar of any zone or Workers &amp; Pages "
"overview."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:79
msgid ""
"Create at <code>My Profile &rarr; API Tokens</code>. Required permission: "
"<code>Account &middot; Cloudflare Pages &middot; Edit</code>."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:86
msgid ""
"The slug only (e.g. <code>my-site</code>), <strong>not</strong> the "
"<code>.pages.dev</code> URL. Create in the CF dashboard with the Direct "
"Upload option."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:93
msgid ""
"<code>main</code> = production deployment. Anything else creates a preview "
"deployment."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:99
msgid "https://my-site.pages.dev or https://www.example.com"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:100
msgid ""
"Where the static site lives publicly. Used to rewrite WP origin URLs in "
"exported HTML and sitemap entries."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:111
msgid "Export Scope"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:112
msgid "Choose which post types and archives to export."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:136
msgid "All published items of selected types are exported."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:143 admin/settings-page.php:401
msgid "Homepage"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:144 admin/settings-page.php:402
msgid "Taxonomy archives"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:145 admin/settings-page.php:403
msgid "Author archives"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:152
msgid "Embed all linked stylesheets into each page"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:153
msgid "Self-contained pages, no external CSS requests."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:157
msgid "Redirect <code>*.pages.dev</code> to live host"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:159
msgid ""
"301-redirect any request hitting <code>&lt;project&gt;.pages.dev</code> to "
"the canonical Public Site URL"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:161
msgid ""
"Adds a Cloudflare Pages Function (<code>functions/_middleware.js</code>) to "
"the deploy that intercepts requests with a <code>.pages.dev</code> hostname "
"and 301-redirects them to your <strong>Public Site URL</strong> (preserving "
"path + query string). Stops Google from indexing the preview URL alongside "
"your real domain."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:162
msgid ""
"Automatically skipped when Public Site URL itself is a <code>.pages.dev</"
"code> URL (e.g. while you're still testing pre-DNS cutover)."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:163
msgid ""
"Counts as a Cloudflare Workers request &mdash; free tier includes 100k/day, "
"sparse <code>.pages.dev</code> traffic costs effectively nothing."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:168
msgid "Rewrite <code>/wp-content/</code> URLs"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:170
msgid ""
"Also rewrite <code>/wp-content/</code> URLs (uploads, themes, plugin assets) "
"to the live host"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:172
msgid ""
"<strong>Default: OFF.</strong> By default, <code>&lt;origin&gt;/wp-"
"content/...</code> URLs are kept pointing at your WordPress origin so media, "
"theme CSS/JS, and plugin assets keep working without bundling gigabytes of "
"files in every deploy."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:173
msgid ""
"<strong>Turn ON only if you've arranged your own proxy / mirror / CDN for "
"<code>/wp-content/*</code> on the live host</strong> &mdash; e.g. a "
"Cloudflare Worker rewriting <code>https://example.com/wp-content/*</code> "
"&rarr; <code>https://dashboard.example.com/wp-content/*</code>, or an Nginx "
"reverse-proxy, or a separate CDN domain. Otherwise images, theme styles and "
"scripts will 404 on the deployed site."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:174
msgid ""
"When ON, schema URLs (<code>og:image</code>, JSON-LD <code>image</code>/"
"<code>logo</code>, <code>thumbnailUrl</code>) and HTML <code>src</code>/"
"<code>srcset</code> point to the live host instead of the dashboard."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:179
msgid "Bundle <code>/wp-content/uploads/</code> into deploy"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:181
msgid ""
"Fetch every <code>/wp-content/uploads/</code> file referenced by the "
"rendered HTML and ship it alongside the static pages"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:183
msgid ""
"<strong>Default: OFF.</strong> Softer alternative to the option above "
"&mdash; only media files (uploads) get rewritten to the live host and "
"bundled into the CF Pages deploy. Theme &amp; plugin assets (CSS/JS/fonts) "
"still load from the WordPress origin."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:184
msgid ""
"Use this when your origin can't be reached from Cloudflare Workers / proxies "
"(shared hosting firewalls, IP allow-lists, etc.). Each rebuild downloads "
"only files referenced from the rendered pages, so cost scales with what's "
"actually used, not the full media library."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:185
msgid ""
"Ignored when \"Rewrite <code>/wp-content/</code> URLs\" above is ON (that "
"setting already rewrites everything)."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:190
msgid "Bundle self-hosted fonts"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:192
msgid ""
"Ship <code>@font-face</code> fonts served from your WordPress host alongside "
"the static pages and point their URLs at the live host"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:194
msgid ""
"<strong>Default: ON.</strong> A self-hosted font (a theme webfont, Astra's "
"local Google Fonts at <code>wp-content/astra-local-fonts/</code>, an icon "
"font) whose <code>src</code> still points at your WordPress origin is a "
"cross-origin request once the page is served from <code>*.pages.dev</code>. "
"Browsers fetch fonts in CORS mode, and the origin doesn't send an "
"<code>Access-Control-Allow-Origin</code> header, so the font is blocked and "
"you get a fallback typeface."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:195
msgid ""
"With this on, every <code>.woff2 / .woff / .ttf / .otf / .eot</code> file "
"referenced from the rendered pages and served from your own host is fetched, "
"bundled into the deploy, and its URL rewritten to the Public Site URL "
"&mdash; so it loads same-origin and the CORS error disappears. Third-party "
"fonts (Google Fonts on <code>fonts.gstatic.com</code>, etc.) already send "
"CORS headers and are left untouched."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:196
msgid ""
"Ignored when \"Rewrite <code>/wp-content/</code> URLs\" above is ON (that "
"already rewrites fonts along with everything else)."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:201
msgid "Extra paths to include"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:211
msgid ""
"<strong>One path per line, relative to your WordPress root.</strong> Point "
"this at files or folders that should be shipped inside the Cloudflare Pages "
"deploy even though the crawler never sees them in the rendered HTML &mdash; "
"a plugin's icon font (e.g. Elementor's Font Awesome at <code>wp-content/"
"plugins/elementor/assets/lib/font-awesome</code>), a webfont directory, a "
"downloadable PDF."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:212
msgid ""
"A whole folder is copied recursively; a single file is copied as-is; a "
"trailing wildcard (<code>wp-content/uploads/2025/*.pdf</code>) is expanded. "
"Bundled files under <code>/wp-content/</code> get their URLs pointed at the "
"live host so the deployed page loads the bundled copy; everything else stays "
"on origin."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:213
msgid ""
"You can enter a path relative to <code>wp-content/</code> too (<code>astra-"
"local-fonts</code> instead of <code>wp-content/astra-local-fonts</code>) "
"&mdash; if it isn't found at the WordPress root, the plugin looks under "
"<code>wp-content/</code> automatically."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:214
msgid ""
"Read straight off local disk, so no origin firewall to worry about. Paths "
"are confined to the WordPress root; anything escaping it via <code>..</code> "
"or a symlink is skipped and logged. Capped at 5,000 files / 200&nbsp;MB per "
"rebuild."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:226
msgid "Performance"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:227
msgid "Core Web Vitals tweaks applied to the rendered HTML."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:233
msgid "Featured image priority"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:235
msgid "Add <code>fetchpriority=\"high\"</code> to the post's featured image"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:237
msgid ""
"Also sets <code>loading=\"eager\"</code> and <code>decoding=\"async\"</"
"code>. Helps the browser identify the LCP element earlier &mdash; improves "
"Core Web Vitals. Works with any theme that uses <code>the_post_thumbnail()</"
"code> or <code>get_the_post_thumbnail()</code>."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:242
msgid "Render origin override"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:246
msgid ""
"<strong>Leave blank unless rebuilds are slow.</strong> The export fetches "
"every page over HTTP from your site's own URL. When your domain runs behind "
"a CDN/proxy (e.g. Cloudflare), each of those requests leaves the server and "
"comes back &mdash; with hundreds of pages that round-trip dominates the "
"rebuild time."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:247
msgid ""
"Set this to a host that points at WordPress <em>directly on this server</em> "
"(usually <code>http://127.0.0.1</code>, or <code>http://127.0.0.1:8080</"
"code> if PHP listens on another port) and the crawl stays on the box. The "
"plugin keeps your real domain in the <code>Host</code> header, so WordPress "
"still serves the correct site/language. TLS verification is skipped for the "
"override only (a loopback cert won't match the public host)."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:248
msgid ""
"Applies to page renders, inlined CSS, mirrored sitemaps, and bundled "
"uploads. Only URLs on your origin host are redirected; everything else is "
"fetched unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:260
msgid "SEO Metadata"
msgstr ""

#: admin/settings-page.php:261
msgid ""
